{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1075985-sidereals-resplendent-destinies-and-demon-the-descent-covers","id":1075985,"title":"Sidereals, Resplendent Destinies, and Demon: the Descent Covers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-10T11:27:14-07:00","id":1075985,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon6.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Sidereals, Resplendent Destinies, and Demon: the Descent Covers","content":"Let's take one of the new dev's quotes and pick it to the bones until Ex3 Sidereals comes out or we grow bored:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1070860#post1070860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Astrology rules are still a ways off, but when I was reading Demon: The Descent, I was struck by how well the mechanical implementation of Cover would fit resplendent destinies.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I know nothing about Demon: the Descent, I had to google what a <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Cover\" target=\"_blank\">Demon's cover</a> was.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Wolf Wiki</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> A Cover is a human identity used by the Unchained. Much more than a simple human disguise, when she first Falls a demon's Cover is the remnants of the Infrastructure that supported her as an angel. A Cover is much more than a backstory and a few props, though. When she Fell, the demon interfaced with reality rather than the God-Machine and wrote her disguise into the world.<br /> Demons have entirely human bodies, fully-detailed backgrounds, relationships, possessions, jobs-whatever was needed for their Cover. The people &quot;related&quot; to the demon don't realize that anything's wrong. In some cases, they didn't even exist until she Fell.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is what I want with a Resplendent Destiny. I want my PC to slip into an existing social group and not have to come up with weird excuses as to why they suddenly showed up. I want the Social group to believe the Sidereals has been there for years. Yes, I know Sidereals get a dice bonus for those situations, but that isn't the same as &quot;What are you talking about? Lin and I grew up together.&quot; The idea of people not even existing until a cover is created is kind of cool, but I imagine this part of Cover won't make it into game. If it does, the Sidereal will most likely accrue paradox for creating new people on the Loom.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Wolf Wiki</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cover can be damaged if a demon deviates too sharply from her human life. The most powerful demonic magical abilities shake Cover, risking exposure. As a demon grows in power, becoming more connected to the universe, her Cover may develop glitches \u2014 obviously inhuman traits like metallic skin or a need to drink mercury, strange emanations of power such as damping radio signals, or bizarre behavioral tics and compulsions like a need to remove the eyes from photographs in case the God-Machine sees her through them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this idea SO much better than the paradox table. Strange things happen around the Sidereal with high levels of paradox. A shattered cup lies on the floor, but is still in the Sidereal's hand unbroken. A strange child follows the Sidereal around. No one knows where she came from.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Wolf Wiki</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cover can be replaced. Demons can learn to steal the Infrastructure of angels or take a human soul and &quot;move into&quot; the life it vacated. Demons grow to the point that they can maintain more than one Cover simultaneously, switching between disguises. If Cover is stripped away entirely, the demon has to run. Trapped in her true form, desperate to find a new Cover she can move into, the fugitive has to face groups of angels attempting to capture her before she can go to ground once more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Identity stealing has always been in the Lunar's wheelhouse more than the Sidereals. With each splat growing to take up more narrative space, maybe a Sidereal can take over an Innkeeper's place for a week until the Solar Circle has passed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Wolf Wiki</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demons, as the result of having been created by an unfeeling, nearly all-encompassing machine, have as much moral sense after the Fall as a copper gear. A human\u2019s grossest sin could be something a demon considers laudable in himself, and he isn\u2019t wrong. However, by taking Covers, a Demon slowly forms a semblance of Morality thanks to residues of their former owners. Demons often integrate aspects of their human fa\u00e7ade into themselves whether they want to or not.<br /> As a result, most demons have no clear Morality score. It depends instead on their defining Virtue or Vice that they have adopted during their Descent, as well as their chosen Aspiration, and is thus highly individual.</div> </div> </div> </div>While Sidereals aren't unfeeling inhuman monsters like Demons, I wonder if a Resplendent Destiny could carry intimacies with it. For example, the Sidereal who took the Innkeeper's place now has a temporary intimacy for the Innkeeper's children.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":".  Removing Wiki Links 04-10-2017, 04:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T13:17:37-07:00","id":1076066,"title":"","content":"Yes! It reappeared! Note to self: When copying from Wiki, remove all the links to avoid the forum spam trap.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T14:09:13-07:00","id":1076096,"title":"","content":"DtD note: demons aren't inherently unfeeling or amoral. In fact, a lot of them fall because the God-Machine wants them to do something they can't stomach. Their morality (small m) is largely accumulated by observation and lived experience, rather than as a mystical effect of Cover.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T14:23:13-07:00","id":1076111,"title":"","content":"It sounds a bit invasive into people's lives and selves in a way that I'm not totally comfortable with being the Sidereal baselines... (Though I think is a thing they could do.)<br /> <br /> I mean, for a game of being a demon (of sorts), I can see you can go straight to the level of warping people's lives, or casually writing their soul and memories into being, with all the existential horror those implies, all for a cover identity. But to play a Sidereal is not to play some transcendent horror-wonder from a higher heaven-hell dimension who has intruded into our reality and seeks to conceal itself from that which would hunt and discover it. Sidereals are human men and women. That's the baseline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T14:36:33-07:00","id":1076119,"title":"","content":"*screaming internally*<br /> Oh gods yes!<br /> <br /> I've been rolling DtD Covers in my head in relation to Sidereals for a while now, except I'm not in a position to do anything about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T14:38:06-07:00","id":1076121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1075985-sidereals-resplendent-destinies-and-demon-the-descent-covers?p=1076096#post1076096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">DtD note: demons aren't inherently unfeeling or amoral. In fact, a lot of them fall because the God-Machine wants them to do something they can't stomach. Their morality (small m) is largely accumulated by observation and lived experience, rather than as a mystical effect of Cover.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the clarification! I'll admit I wrote from ignorance of the DtD setting. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1075985-sidereals-resplendent-destinies-and-demon-the-descent-covers?p=1076111#post1076111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It sounds a bit invasive into people's lives and selves in a way that I'm not totally comfortable with being the Sidereal baselines... (Though I think is a thing they could do.)<br /> <br /> I mean, for a game of being a demon (of sorts), I can see you can go straight to the level of warping people's lives, or casually writing their soul and memories into being, with all the existential horror those implies, all for a cover identity. But to play a Sidereal is not to play some transcendent horror-wonder from a higher heaven-hell dimension who has intruded into our reality and seeks to conceal itself from that which would hunt and discover it. Sidereals are human men and women. That's the baseline.</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume you are talking about the &quot;insert yourself into a social group&quot; idea. As Sidereals are human, I imagine it is heartbreaking to have all these people love you as a friend and to know that it is all false. Your friendship is a lie. When the RD ends, you will be forgotten. You could go back and start over, but Arcane Fate makes developing friendships so difficult.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T14:45:28-07:00","id":1076127,"title":"","content":"Being familiar with both Demon: the Descent and Exalted, it's impossible to miss the parallels and the way the two concepts might inform one another. Demon is the CofD gameline which straight up has Avoidance Kata in the corebook power list (as Four Minutes Ago), not to mention various other powers like Force Relationship.<br /> <br /> They're obviously not the exact same, nor should they be, but I'm pretty comfortable to hear the Demon book is passing under Vance's eyes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T15:15:59-07:00","id":1076140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1075985-sidereals-resplendent-destinies-and-demon-the-descent-covers?p=1076121#post1076121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assume you are talking about the &quot;insert yourself into a social group&quot; idea. As Sidereals are human, I imagine it is heartbreaking to have all these people love you as a friend and to know that it is all false. Your friendship is a lie. When the RD ends, you will be forgotten. You could go back and start over, but Arcane Fate makes developing friendships so difficult.</div> </div> </div> </div>Trying to articulate a little better, my image of the Sidereals is more that... <br /> <br /> In the first and highest age of man, the Sidereals saw a threat which would burn their world to ash and bone. They broke the fates, and removed themselves from identity and history, to give them the matchless disguise and stealth to baffle and defeat an enemy that could, would, see anything coming.<br /> <br /> The legacy of that is a curse and exile. What Resplendent Destinies do is give them a choice and an option of how to respond to that; they can choose to use them to lead a rootless existence, conning humanity, living through mask under mask, building false selves to live a semblance of a human life, using identities only as a means to an ends.. or they can choose to build an identity that's as close as they can to true, and build relationships around that which are close to genuine and real as they can. <br /> <br /> There's a question there; How do you respond when you lose who you are, and you can rebuild identity, with effort, but never truly be known by others for who you are? What path do you embrace? With a wrinkle that makes this whole dilemma much more interesting, if your work calls on you to be a spy, to be a cipher, is the moral choice necessarily the one that we would think is closest to authenticity and honesty?<br /> <br /> Crucially, in either sense it's a response that they choose and which we can respect in that they've worked to build it. They've made those relationships from ground up.<br /> <br /> I think what I don't like so much in the excerpts in the OP is it feels like there is the suggestion of taking away the choice, and the effort and sweat, from them - the equivalent idea seems more like it would be one where Resplendent Destiny reaches out and reforms reality to create an identity for them. If that means it takes people's lives and selves from them, reforms them in different patterns, they can choose how they feel about it, but they're not really choosing at root in the same way. There's a rather passive aspect of personal horror to that (of the experience of being a reality disruptive horror against your will) that seems quite different to me than what I'd think Sidereals are going for.<br /> <br /> (I'm sure this is a little pretentious. More than a little. Quite a lot, even.).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T17:11:37-07:00","id":1076190,"title":"","content":"As someone who has played and read a lot of Demon, I think that Cover is a really excellent inspiration for how to make Resplendent Destinies make sense and be cool.<br /> <br /> That it's slightly flawed is also an important part of it, though. I think that part is definitely something to keep for the Exalted version, not to make Sidereals jump through hoops but to give it some interesting impetus in gameplay and to highlight the unreality of the Resplendent Destiny in a fun sort of way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T20:22:54-07:00","id":1076262,"title":"","content":"As it happens, Sidereals were a loose inspiration for demons. I don't think I ever considered Resplendent Destinies specifically, but I probably should have. But agents of the Heaven-establishment whose abilities work on backdoors in the infrastructure of reality has obvious overlap....<br /> <br /> I think Destinies having Intimacies would be a pretty cool idea. One thing I didn't have time to make work in DtD was giving Covers their own Aspirations, but I think it would have worked nicely with a bit more development.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T07:22:55-07:00","id":1076470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1075985-sidereals-resplendent-destinies-and-demon-the-descent-covers?p=1076262#post1076262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As it happens, Sidereals were a loose inspiration for demons. I don't think I ever considered Resplendent Destinies specifically, but I probably should have. But agents of the Heaven-establishment whose abilities work on backdoors in the infrastructure of reality has obvious overlap....</div> </div> </div> </div>Somehow, this reminds of The Adjustment Bureau, which could have been such a good movie if only it actually focused on the agents instead of being a by-the-numbers love story.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think Destinies having Intimacies would be a pretty cool idea. </div> </div> </div>Personally I really like the idea of Sidereals keeping (at least) the Ties they make as a reinforcement of the isolation RDs create (also as a distinction from Solar Personae). You have within you lifetimes of experiences with real people, but those experiences never &quot;really&quot; happened, because the person you were never &quot;really&quot; existed.<br /> <br /> I think it lessens the humanity of Sidereals if they can simply cast off e.g. a Defining Tie by taking off a RD. I mean, they should be able to do it through Charms, sure, but maybe not as a base power. I like stories of undercover agents that form real bonds of loyalty / love / friendship, against their &quot;better judgement&quot;, that cause them to question their superiors, their associations and stuff. ( come to think of it, I just described the Fall, didn't I? )<br /> <br /> At least, that with my current working model of Sidereals. For all I know their implementation (and/or that of RDs) will change enough for the opposite to be just as compelling.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T07:34:20-07:00","id":1076477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1075985-sidereals-resplendent-destinies-and-demon-the-descent-covers?p=1076262#post1076262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As it happens, Sidereals were a loose inspiration for demons. I don't think I ever considered Resplendent Destinies specifically, but I probably should have. But agents of the Heaven-establishment whose abilities work on backdoors in the infrastructure of reality has obvious overlap....</div> </div> </div> </div>Suddenly Demon: the Descent is way more interesting to me. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1075985-sidereals-resplendent-destinies-and-demon-the-descent-covers?p=1076262#post1076262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Destinies having Intimacies would be a pretty cool idea. One thing I didn't have time to make work in DtD was giving Covers their own Aspirations, but I think it would have worked nicely with a bit more development.</div> </div> </div> </div>Resplendent Destinies with Intimacies would have interesting implications for Ex3's Social Combat System. You do read intentions and get the false RD intimacy instead of one of the Sidereal's real Intimacies. A Sidereal on a Mission to save a town may not care about the town itself. Yet, the Sidereal could create a RD that does care about the town and use that intimacy to boost their Resolve.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T07:43:20-07:00","id":1076483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1075985-sidereals-resplendent-destinies-and-demon-the-descent-covers?p=1076470#post1076470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it lessens the humanity of Sidereals if they can simply cast off e.g. a Defining Tie by taking off a RD. I mean, they should be able to do it through Charms, sure, but maybe not as a base power. I like stories of undercover agents that form real bonds of loyalty / love / friendship, against their &quot;better judgement&quot;, that cause them to question their superiors, their associations and stuff. ( come to think of it, I just described the Fall, didn't I? )</div> </div> </div> </div>Ideally, a Sidereal should be able to cast off Intimacies built into an RD. It is what the Elder Sidereals expect a Sidereal to do when they are done with the mission. Or when a Mission changes and now the Sidereal has to help the invaders pillage the village. <br /> <br /> However, there should be a risk of an intimacy bleeding over into the Sidereal's real Intimacies. Maybe the longer the Sidereal wears the RD, the more likely they start to identify with the people the interact with. It should be a risk, not something that happens by default. Otherwise you'd get Sidereals abandoning the Bureau of Destiny on their first mission. <br /> <br /> Now that I have written this out, I realize this is what the majority of the Sidereal Integrity Charms do. It ties a Sidereal to a cause and allow them to follow though without all those &quot;annoying&quot; emotional entanglements. I'll have to think about this more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T07:43:30-07:00","id":1076484,"title":"","content":"What if a RD-specific Intimacies could only be created at the RD's inception (and were unalterable maybe?) while any further intimacies went directly to the Sidereal?<br /> Would have that on-the-job advantage of caring about your goal while keeping the human getting-too-attached aspect.<br /> <br /> ninja-edit:<br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1075985-sidereals-resplendent-destinies-and-demon-the-descent-covers?p=1076483#post1076483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ideally, a Sidereal should be able to cast off Intimacies built into an RD. It is what the Elder Sidereals expect a Sidereal to do when they are done with the mission.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, but I also think that it shouldn't be a realistic expectation for a starting Sidereal. I see it as one of those &quot;my spy-master boss that's been doing this for 300 years expects me to be a cold-hearted monster&quot; situations where you <i>eventually</i> get there, but is <i>really</i> hard at first (unless you spec for it).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 04-11-2017, 10:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T08:42:34-07:00","id":1076518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1075985-sidereals-resplendent-destinies-and-demon-the-descent-covers?p=1076484#post1076484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if a RD-specific Intimacies could only be created at the RD's inception (and were unalterable maybe?) while any further intimacies went directly to the Sidereal?<br /> Would have that on-the-job advantage of caring about your goal while keeping the human getting-too-attached aspect.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is actually the senario I was thinking of. You set intimacies at the creation of the RD and can use those Intimacies to bump up your Resolve. But if you get swayed by an argument that is better than your resolve, then YOU get a new intimacy. <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1075985-sidereals-resplendent-destinies-and-demon-the-descent-covers?p=1076484#post1076484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree, but I also think that it shouldn't be a realistic expectation for a starting Sidereal. I see it as one of those &quot;my spy-master boss that's been doing this for 300 years expects me to be a cold-hearted monster&quot; situations where you <i>eventually</i> get there, but is <i>really</i> hard at first (unless you spec for it).</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Got to start with easy missions about saving orphans first. Then you find out your spy-master boss has been killing orphans for the Bureau, but for reasons of Fate. Then you get to decide if those reasons are the right reasons or the Bureau is full of bullshit. <br /> <br /> Good times. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T12:01:46-07:00","id":1076612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1075985-sidereals-resplendent-destinies-and-demon-the-descent-covers?p=1076483#post1076483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ideally, a Sidereal should be able to cast off Intimacies built into an RD. It is what the Elder Sidereals expect a Sidereal to do when they are done with the mission. Or when a Mission changes and now the Sidereal has to help the invaders pillage the village.<br /> <br /> However, there should be a risk of an intimacy bleeding over into the Sidereal's real Intimacies. Maybe the longer the Sidereal wears the RD, the more likely they start to identify with the people the interact with. It should be a risk, not something that happens by default. Otherwise you'd get Sidereals abandoning the Bureau of Destiny on their first mission.<br /> <br /> Now that I have written this out, I realize this is what the majority of the Sidereal Integrity Charms do. It ties a Sidereal to a cause and allow them to follow though without all those &quot;annoying&quot; emotional entanglements. I'll have to think about this more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Moving intimacies off of the RD and onto your character should be one of the major effects of paradox. It's simultaneously meaningful and not-gameplay-stalling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T12:17:10-07:00","id":1076620,"title":"","content":"I'm sure there are aspects of mechanical representation that could cross over, but I find the themes inherent to Demon to be really unlike Sidereals, and feel as though making them aspects of resplendent destinies would be very distracting.<br /> <br /> Now, for <i>Getimians</i>, that's a horse of a different colour.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T13:08:35-07:00","id":1076638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AtG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1075985-sidereals-resplendent-destinies-and-demon-the-descent-covers?p=1076612#post1076612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Moving intimacies off of the RD and onto your character should be one of the major effects of paradox. It's simultaneously meaningful and not-gameplay-stalling.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ... Oh my god that's so obvious and awesome and easy <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T13:55:30-07:00","id":1076655,"title":"","content":"I think the most I'd look to Demon for inspiration would be mechanical concepts like how to approach Cover for Resplendent Destinies. I think Pacts aren't necessary, though they might give some ideas for how to do Astrology possibly, I dunno.<br /> <br /> Otherwise I think the concepts of a lot of Embeds could make great inspiration for subtle kinds of Sidereal Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T14:10:51-07:00","id":1076659,"title":"","content":"Something like every [Essence] days or weeks, you make a wp roll to see if you gain one of your RD's Intimacies. This way older Sids are more jaded and find it easier to discard cover after cover, but a younger fate ninja staying longer in one particular RD is at risk to go native.<br /> <br /> I like the paradox effect of &quot;immediatly gain one or more intimacies from your RD&quot; too ^^.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ultimate Jade-Screened Exalted Scholar, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304239-my-next-campaign-tdhr-peach\" target=\"_blank\">THDR : Future Dragon-Blooded campaign</a>, and other links.<br /> If you like Ex3, you can support <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/holdenshearer\" target=\"_blank\">Holden</a> on Patreon!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/541-letipex","name":"LeTipex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"902"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T16:12:27-07:00","id":1076695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1075985-sidereals-resplendent-destinies-and-demon-the-descent-covers?p=1076470#post1076470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I really like the idea of Sidereals keeping (at least) the Ties they make as a reinforcement of the isolation RDs create (also as a distinction from Solar Personae). You have within you lifetimes of experiences with real people, but those experiences never &quot;really&quot; happened, because the person you were never &quot;really&quot; existed.<br /> <br /> I think it lessens the humanity of Sidereals if they can simply cast off e.g. a Defining Tie by taking off a RD. I mean, they should be able to do it through Charms, sure</div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereal Integrity Charms, in the House of the Sword, under the sign of Endings.<br /> <br /> Saturn's executioner's sword, for bringing an end to all things. Such as Intimacies which have outlived their usefulness.<br /> <br /> Fitting that the Endbringers would be the Viziers most capable of leaving old identities behind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T16:19:48-07:00","id":1076698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1075985-sidereals-resplendent-destinies-and-demon-the-descent-covers?p=1076695#post1076695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sidereal Integrity Charms, in the House of the Sword, under the sign of Endings.<br /> <br /> Saturn's executioner's sword, for bringing an end to all things. Such as Intimacies which have outlived their usefulness.<br /> <br /> Fitting that the Endbringers would be the Viziers most capable of leaving old identities behind.</div> </div> </div> </div>All of my yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T18:12:29-07:00","id":1076735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1075985-sidereals-resplendent-destinies-and-demon-the-descent-covers?p=1076121#post1076121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As Sidereals are human, I imagine it is heartbreaking to have all these people love you as a friend and to know that it is all false.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the character. My last character gave precisely zero fucks about that sort of thing, and created, discarded and burned out identities as the situation warranted. They were a tool, to be used and discarded as needed. Only about half her RDs even had an identity attached; the others were purely power batteries (having a Key destiny primed for an emergency bolt hole to Yu-Shan is pretty handy). She also made heavy use of Subordinate Inspiration Technique to bypass having to directly interact with people entirely. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1075985-sidereals-resplendent-destinies-and-demon-the-descent-covers?p=1076695#post1076695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fitting that the Endbringers would be the Viziers most capable of leaving old identities behind.</div> </div> </div> </div>If we are to presume different levels of ability in discarding RDs, which I don't necessarily agree with, I would think that Secrets would be pretty good at it too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T18:23:57-07:00","id":1076738,"title":"","content":"Personally, I find resplendent destinies to be more distinct and interesting when they're a kind of aura that people generally relate to by projecting their own expectations on.<br /> <br /> \u200bI suppose I could see a form of paradox in which the narrative glitches to cause some of those expectations to actually infect your personality, but I wouldn't want a starting premise in which a resplendency already constitutes an alternate personality with Intimacies.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'm also very attached to the image of Sidereals not being universal masters of disguise so much as Arcane Fate giving them so little presence that the bar for an effective disguise is ludicrously low for them.<br /> <br /> \u200bI think there's something interesting to the idea of them creating a cover identity by fabricating a life for themselves, but that's something I think would work a lot better as a function of marshalling the resources of the Heavenly Bureaucracy rather than taking advantage of Arcane Fate.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat gets to the heart of why I don't think Cover translates very effectively; they're not the fugitives, they're the eye in the sky.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T18:54:09-07:00","id":1076746,"title":"","content":"False Identities are a big part of Spies and that is totally in the Sidereal\u2019s wheelhouse. Functionality, I'd prefer RD to have a bit more meat to them than &quot;you get a dice bonus, can interact with people like non-Sidereal PCs, and a whole bunch of powers you can't use because you didn't get enough successes on you Astrology rolls.&quot; <br /> <br /> In my observations, no Sidereal player is happy with RD as they are in Ex2. For the amount of effort it takes to calculate all the rolls, you get little out of it. I had a fellow player refer to Astrology as &quot;Destiny Taxes&quot;. I know Sidereals are supposed to be drowning in obscure paperwork and red tape, but the game need to recreate that experience in dice rolling? <br /> <br /> I want RD to be more than you are a bit less forgettable now! Hell, maybe with integrity charms you can submerge you true identity into your RD and be like the Doctor and John Smith in Human Nature/Family of Blood - <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Human_Nature_(Doctor_Who\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Huma...re_(Doctor_Who</a>)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T20:42:54-07:00","id":1076782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1075985-sidereals-resplendent-destinies-and-demon-the-descent-covers?p=1076140#post1076140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Trying to articulate a little better, my image of the Sidereals is more that...<br /> <br /> In the first and highest age of man, the Sidereals saw a threat which would burn their world to ash and bone. They broke the fates, and removed themselves from identity and history, to give them the matchless disguise and stealth to baffle and defeat an enemy that could, would, see anything coming.<br /> <br /> The legacy of that is a curse and exile. What Resplendent Destinies do is give them a choice and an option of how to respond to that; they can choose to use them to lead a rootless existence, conning humanity, living through mask under mask, building false selves to live a semblance of a human life, using identities only as a means to an ends.. or they can choose to build an identity that's as close as they can to true, and build relationships around that which are close to genuine and real as they can.<br /> <br /> There's a question there; How do you respond when you lose who you are, and you can rebuild identity, with effort, but never truly be known by others for who you are? What path do you embrace? With a wrinkle that makes this whole dilemma much more interesting, if your work calls on you to be a spy, to be a cipher, is the moral choice necessarily the one that we would think is closest to authenticity and honesty?<br /> <br /> Crucially, in either sense it's a response that they choose and which we can respect in that they've worked to build it. They've made those relationships from ground up.<br /> <br /> I think what I don't like so much in the excerpts in the OP is it feels like there is the suggestion of taking away the choice, and the effort and sweat, from them - the equivalent idea seems more like it would be one where Resplendent Destiny reaches out and reforms reality to create an identity for them. If that means it takes people's lives and selves from them, reforms them in different patterns, they can choose how they feel about it, but they're not really choosing at root in the same way. There's a rather passive aspect of personal horror to that (of the experience of being a reality disruptive horror against your will) that seems quite different to me than what I'd think Sidereals are going for.<br /> <br /> (I'm sure this is a little pretentious. More than a little. Quite a lot, even.).</div> </div> </div> </div>In Demon, each Cover has a rating which determines just how &quot;real&quot; it is. At low ratings, you might have the 4th apartment on a floor that only has three of them, a closet full of the exact same clothing (down to the rips and stains), and your coworkers know you as &quot;just this guy, you know?&quot; One of the things you can get from roleplaying your Cover well, making deals with humans, and other stuff is Cover XP which can be used to make your cover more and more real. Even at Cover 10, you're living a lie, but it's one you've had to work hard to make as real as possible.<br /> <br /> While I have no idea how Sidereals are gonna work, I wanted to note that &quot;create relationships (and people) from the ground up&quot; and &quot;you have to work hard to turn a fake life into a real one&quot; are not actually incompatible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T00:52:16-07:00","id":1076846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1075985-sidereals-resplendent-destinies-and-demon-the-descent-covers?p=1076746#post1076746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">False Identities are a big part of Spies and that is totally in the Sidereal\u2019s wheelhouse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but I like how resplendent destinies in the manner I describe them represent both that, and the side to them as mystics.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Functionality, I'd prefer RD to have a bit more meat to them than &quot;you get a dice bonus, can interact with people like non-Sidereal PCs, and a whole bunch of powers you can't use because you didn't get enough successes on you Astrology rolls.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI'm just saying that there are a few things that better mechanics could implement, and stating my own preference and aversion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T06:22:34-07:00","id":1076927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1075985-sidereals-resplendent-destinies-and-demon-the-descent-covers?p=1076846#post1076846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bI'm just saying that there are a few things that better mechanics could implement, and stating my own preference and aversion.</div> </div> </div> </div>No worries. I didn't mean for my tone to come off as antagonistical. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T09:27:46-07:00","id":1077021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1075985-sidereals-resplendent-destinies-and-demon-the-descent-covers?p=1076746#post1076746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my observations, no Sidereal player is happy with RD as they are in Ex2. For the amount of effort it takes to calculate all the rolls, you get little out of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd have to see if I could find it, but I worked up a system where you could perform astrology by rolling 1d3. It worked on the assumption that, since the intervals for astrology rolls was so long, in all but the most extenuating circumstances you could reasonably assume infinite time, infinite motes and maximum preparation on each roll. Thus, the only point of variance that couldn't be pre-calculated was the Performance roll...<i>but</i>, since every Sidereal was required to have a rating in Performance (three dots, I believe), you could minimally invest in Peformance (a two dot Sidereal Astrology specialty and the Second Performance Excellency/being Serenity caste) and be at least competent. Depending on how well you rolled, the Performance roll usually added...you guessed it, one to three points on your effect roll.<br /> <br /> So you could save a lot of effort by pre-calculating your minimum Effect dice, then when it came time to actually do Astrology you just rolled 1d3 and your Paradox and Bob's your uncle.<br /> <br /> And in general, I'm not crazy of Resplendant Destinies having the ability to infect a Sidereal with any fake intimacies they establish for it. We've already had two editions where being a Sidereal was essentially a punishment and your own powers screwed you over in creative and malicious ways. I'd really like to buck the trend this time around. I mean, stop me if I'm being too crazy here, but what if a power <i>didn't have downsides</i>?<br /> <br /> Madness? Chaos? Forty years of darkness? Up is down, black is white, earthquakes, volcanoes, the dead rising from the grave?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T09:37:25-07:00","id":1077027,"title":"","content":"I like the idea that an RD can &quot;create&quot; people, as a function of how strong the false identity is, but for Sidereals I would interpret it as a a specific case of the more general phenomenon of standing up to some degree of scrutiny. Like, if you ask around about the Sidereal, someone might say &quot;Bill? Yeah, known him for years. He's married to my cousin Louise.&quot; except that &quot;Bill&quot; didn't exist before yesterday, and Louise <i>still</i> doesn't. But just like the RD fabricated the idea that Bill had always been around, it also fabricated supporting evidence (including the Louise and various relationships people may have to her) in everyone's minds as well.<br /> <br /> As far as actual, tangible evidence (like the fake apartment mentioned above, or a <i>real</i> version of the &quot;cousin&quot; from the Bill example), I think that's perfect space for Resplendencies to play in, whether it's commissioning the Pattern Spiders to find an unused room somewhere that everyone will believe is your apartment, or casting a little god in the role of a person who doesn't exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 04-12-2017, 12:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T14:36:23-07:00","id":1077927,"title":"","content":"I was thinking about this again today, and about Blackwell's great suggestions for Resplendencies (I think they really work well to square the circle between what people are looking for in the Cover mechanic with what Sidereals are), and a couple other ideas sprung to mind as variations on the theme &quot;casting a little god in the role of a person who doesn't exist&quot; (and I feel bound to bump this day old thread to inflict these ideas on the world):<br /> <br /> - Casting a demon or Fair Folk in that position, as an extension of the Sidereal's charms to con chaos and their Exalted power to bind demons. Heaven is often chronically short of resources! The rolls of glorious divinity cannot always spare one of their number. Why not put out a contact and make a deal? Perhaps a Blood Ape with an illusion bound around to appear human might *perhaps* eat a few kittens from time to time, but nothing could go seriously wrong, surely?<br /> <br /> - For Getimians, if they have anything akin to Arcane Fate, finding the threads of people written out of Fate, and literally writing them back in as personal relationships running off the Getimian's Loom. Could strike a nice balance between being both altruistic and roughly in keeping with their &quot;mission&quot; to correct destiny's injustice... and questionably self serving.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T14:57:37-07:00","id":1077946,"title":"","content":"So, is everybody really this comfortable with ignoring the Astrological (as in &quot;constellation-related&quot;) aspects of Resplendent Destinies? Because I'm seeing a lot of discussion about RDs as disguises and as a means for hiding out among the <i>hoi polloi</i>, but very little consideration of the concept of RDs as astrological archetypes. <br /> <br /> I may not be a fan of Creation's version of the zodiac (do they really need a Mast <i>and</i> a Pillar? And how uninspiring does an arrangement of stars have to be to bring to mind &quot;The Rising Smoke?&quot;), but I am extremely fond of Sidereal Astrology as a concept, of each Resplendent Destiny conforming to a zodiacal archetype, and even of the quirky, inconsistent power levels of the RD powers.*<br /> <br /> I'm familiar with D:tD's Cover mechanic, and though it's fine for Demons, I'm just not feeling it at all for Sidereals and Exalted. Demons have to fear the all-seeing eye of their Big Bad finding them, so Cover makes sense. Sidereals <i>are</i> the all-seeing eye, and they only have to worry about being unmasked by their peers or their lessers. Such thorough identity-weaving seems unnecessary, IMHO.<br /> <br /> <i>*And by inconsistent, I mean that it ranges from &quot;If you act like a tyrant while captaining, your men won't question your orders!&quot; to &quot;oh yeah, you summon Adorjan.&quot;</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1536-39steps","name":"39Steps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1536_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T15:29:12-07:00","id":1077974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>39Steps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1075985-sidereals-resplendent-destinies-and-demon-the-descent-covers?p=1077946#post1077946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm familiar with D:tD's Cover mechanic, and though it's fine for Demons, I'm just not feeling it at all for Sidereals and Exalted. Demons have to fear the all-seeing eye of their Big Bad finding them, so Cover makes sense. Sidereals <i>are</i> the all-seeing eye, and they only have to worry about being unmasked by their peers or their lessers. Such thorough identity-weaving seems unnecessary, IMHO.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, and I think Demons are more comparable to Getimians, anyway. The Sidereals are the Angels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T15:52:56-07:00","id":1077984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>39Steps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1075985-sidereals-resplendent-destinies-and-demon-the-descent-covers?p=1077946#post1077946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, is everybody really this comfortable with ignoring the Astrological (as in &quot;constellation-related&quot;) aspects of Resplendent Destinies? Because I'm seeing a lot of discussion about RDs as disguises and as a means for hiding out among the <i>hoi polloi</i>, but very little consideration of the concept of RDs as astrological archetypes.</div> </div> </div> </div> Right now, they're both; the identity you create aligns with the archetype of the College you created it from. I don't see why that would have to change if the mechanics associated with the identity were shored up a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T16:08:31-07:00","id":1078000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1075985-sidereals-resplendent-destinies-and-demon-the-descent-covers?p=1077927#post1077927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Casting a demon or Fair Folk in that position, as an extension of the Sidereal's charms to con chaos and their Exalted power to bind demons. Heaven is often chronically short of resources! The rolls of glorious divinity cannot always spare one of their number. Why not put out a contact and make a deal? Perhaps a Blood Ape with an illusion bound around to appear human might *perhaps* eat a few kittens from time to time, but nothing could go seriously wrong, surely?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's great and Sidereal-y, but I'd want some carrot/stick mechanics to make it clear why a Sidereal would ever actually <i>do</i> that. They tend to be arrogant, but not reckless. Surely there are enough unemployed gods milling about (and heck, elementals are practically a renewable resource) that an agent of Heaven acting on official business would never need to resort to roping a monster into her Astrology just because there's no one else available. But if there's some kind of concrete situational incentive to use a Fair Folk or Demon rather than a more friendly spirit, then you've seeded an interesting story about hubris. &quot;It was worth the risk&quot; is written on many a Sidereal tombstone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 04-13-2017, 07:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T22:42:22-07:00","id":1078184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>39Steps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1075985-sidereals-resplendent-destinies-and-demon-the-descent-covers?p=1077946#post1077946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, is everybody really this comfortable with ignoring the Astrological (as in &quot;constellation-related&quot;) aspects of Resplendent Destinies? Because I'm seeing a lot of discussion about RDs as disguises and as a means for hiding out among the <i>hoi polloi</i>, but very little consideration of the concept of RDs as astrological archetypes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it's so much ignoring it as not really feeling like it needs any adjustments. The worst criticism I think I can level against the actual constellations and the associated powers is that they're fairly repetitive in places, and I can't really tell if that's due to wanting to cover bases in each caste (like the &quot;can't be found but you only have a small amount of free time in a week&quot; powers) or 75 or so unique powers was too tall an order for a subsystem.<br /> <br /> The mechanics, on the other hand, have always stunk out loud: they're dull, most of them are unnecessary, blessings and curses are completely fiat-driven without even guidelines, the resplendency powers range from completely useless even by Sidereal &quot;You're supposed to be creative and look for edge cases&quot; standards to laughably broken, and to put the shit cherry on the shit sundae treats the entire thing like it's this amazingly useful and overpowered system that you <i>must be punished</i> for using.<br /> <br /> So, ya'know, there's a fair bit more to discuss on that side of things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T22:45:15-07:00","id":1078185,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I think the constellation and stuff are fine and they provide a great flavor and archetypes of people that are cool. RDs anchored by the constellations is the flavor that I'd like to see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}